What is HoneyPot:

Honeypot ek jaal (trap) system hota hai. Yeh jaanbujhkar ek asli device jaisa dikhta hai (Windows XP, Apache server, Router, Printer),
lekin isme koi real data ya real kaam nahi hota. Iska maqsad hai attackers ko attract karna aur unki activity record karna.


=> Kaam kaise karta hai

Honeypot ek fake service chalata hai, jaise SSH (port 22), Telnet (23), HTTP (80), SMB (445).
Attacker ko lagta hai yeh asli, vulnerable machine hai.
Wo scan karta hai, login try karta hai, exploit chalata hai.
Honeypot sab log karta hai: attacker ka IP, username/password, commands, malware, exploit payload.
Asli system ko koi nuksan nahi hota, kyunki yeh sab isolated hai.

=> Example:
python3 main.py device:web:windows:windowsxp nccc 3 ek Windows XP device ka fake profile chalata hai.

1. Honeypot - Decoder compiling: 
matlab yeh attack patterns pehchanne wale decoders load kar raha hai: CVE exploits (Fortinet, Cisco, Struts, PHP), XOR shellcode, base64 payloads, Metasploit patterns.
2. Capture_Packet_started = network traffic capture ho raha hai.
3. Event Manager Started = attack events ko record aur alert karega.
4. Port Scanner Started = port scan detect karega.


. TIA table me alag-alag profiles hain (windowsxp, apache-server, checkpoint firewall, Cisco router, HPLaserJet printer, Openhab). Yeh sab alag-alag fake devices hain jo Power sector testbed ki DMZ me lage hain,
taaki attackers ICS/power infrastructure jaisa target samjhein.

. smb folder ke andar reverse_fake_shell.py, smb32.py, smbetx64.py jaise files hain. Yeh SMB exploits (jaise EternalBlue type) ko emulate karti hain, aur fake shell dikhati hain taaki attacker aage commands chalaye aur uska behaviour record ho.



. Honeypot kyun use karte hain

Naye attacks aur zero-day ka pata chalta hai.
Attacker ke tools aur TTPs (tactics, techniques, procedures) samajh aate hain.
Threat intelligence milti hai: malicious IPs, malware samples.
Early warning system ki tarah kaam karta hai. Honeypot par koi bhi connection suspicious hota hai, kyunki koi legitimate user ise use nahi karta.

. Types

Low-interaction: sirf basic services emulate karta hai (zyada safe, kam detail).
High-interaction: asli OS/service deta hai (zyada detail, zyada risk).
Medium-interaction: aapka jaisa lagta hai, jo fake shell aur protocols emulate karta hai.



